; coverage test for the `commit` keyword: closes a `sandbox` immediately (no dedent needed,
; like `break`) but keeps its content instead of discarding it -- selective export, exactly
; like `load`: only a labelled, non-`local` fact (and the symbols it needs) survives.
load prop
bool C, D

; positive: a labelled fact declared inside the sandbox is still derivable afterward
sandbox
    use C "c-fact"
    commit
C

; negative control: without `commit` (plain `break`), the same kind of fact does NOT survive
sandbox
    use D "d-fact"
    break
expect "ProofError"
    D
;;; Proof checked.
